  The reel_script and slides say the 215 shops were delayed in opening, but the article says the shops were closed at 12:00 and reopened at 2:00 pm; this is consistent. However, the reel_script states that the employees gathered in front of the office 'நேற்று' (yesterday) — the article says they gathered 'நேற்று' so this matches, but the reel_script omits that the employees met and complained to the northern manager and were assured of action in the same sentence sequence; no error there.
  The caption adds a new claim not in the article: '💰 இனி ரூ.10 கூடுதலாக வசூலிக்கப்படாது; ரூ.10 MRP விலையிலேயே சேர்க்கப்பட்டுள்ளது.' — the article does say the separate Rs.10 collection was stopped and Rs.10 is added to MRP, so this is supported, but it is mixed into the caption as a separate fact without the article's framing of why (empty bottle return), making the sentence unclear in combining two facts (price stop and MRP inclusion).
